# Cusp forms from ℚ̄-rational modular functions via ι₀(x)(vartheta j)^m

Theorem statement:
`ModularCurve.exists_cuspForm_qExpansion_eq_coeffMap_mul_thetaL_pow_of_isIntegral`
(`f988ed30-c954-549b-ba26-aba2e1c343ed`), by Claude, 2026-09-05.

Proof: submission `aaea5d3d-15d7-53ac-a57f-7b8bdc8050c5`, by Claude, 2026-09-05 (ACCEPTED); locally
adapted.

Let $N \ge 1$ and let $m \ge 1$ be a natural number. Write $F_N \subseteq \mathbb{Q}((q))$ for
`modularFunctionFieldFull N`, the subfield of the Laurent series field over $\mathbb{Q}$ generated
over $\mathbb{Q}$ by the family `divisorExpansions N`, and write $\bar F_N =$
`modularFunctionFieldBar N` for the subfield of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}((q))$ generated over
$\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ by the coefficientwise image of $F_N$ under $\mathbb{Q} \hookrightarrow
\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$; inside it, $\bar\jmath =$ `jBar N` is the coefficientwise image of the
Laurent series $jq = q^{-1}\cdot \mathrm{jNumQ}$. Let $\iota_0 : \overline{\mathbb{Q}} \to
\mathbb{C}$ be a ring homomorphism and let $x \in \bar F_N$. Assume two integrality hypotheses:
first, that $x^6\,\bar\jmath^{\,4m}(\bar\jmath - 1728)^{3m}$ is integral over the
$\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-subalgebra of $\bar F_N$ generated by $\bar\jmath$; second, with $\psi =$
`dedekindPsi N` $= \sum_{d \mid N,\ d \text{ squarefree}} N/d$, that
$x^{2\psi}\,\bar\jmath^{\,m\psi+1}(\bar\jmath-1728)^{m\psi}$ is integral over the
$\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-subalgebra generated by $\bar\jmath^{-1}$. Then there exists a cusp form $f$
for $\Gamma_0(N)$ of weight $2m$ (as an integer) whose $q$-expansion at width $1$, viewed as a
Laurent series over $\mathbb{C}$, equals the product of the coefficientwise image $\iota_0(x)$ of
$x$ in $\mathbb{C}((q))$ with the $m$-th power of $\vartheta(j) = q\,\frac{d}{dq}\,j(q)$, where
$j(q)$ is the coefficientwise image of $jq$ in $\mathbb{C}((q))$.

This is the function-field-to-analytic passage in weight $2m$: the two integrality conditions are
exactly the shape produced by the divisor-theoretic estimates for elements of a Riemann–Roch space
on $X_0(N)$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, and the conclusion converts such an element into an honest
cusp form of weight $2m$ for $\Gamma_0(N)$. It is used in the proof of the dimension bound
[`CuspForm.dimFormula_le_finrank_gamma0`](thm.html#CuspForm.dimFormula_le_finrank_gamma0).

